 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "hoover washer drier showing EO3 wont drain, ive done the filter its clean. H3DS4965DACE. pump just buzzes. do i need a new pump??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "To answer your question directly: not necessarily yet. A buzzing sound usually means the pump motor is trying to run but can't turn because something is jamming it (like a coin, button, or hair tie) caught in the impeller. If you clear that blockage and it spins freely again, the pump might be fine. Please do this check: switch off and unplug the machine first. With the filter already removed, shine a torch into the housing and try to turn the small plastic fan blades inside with your finger. Does it spin freely, is it stuck by debris, or are the blades broken? This will tell us if we just need to clear a jam or if the pump itself has failed."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "done that. impeller spins totally freely, no resistance at all, feels like its not connected to anything. torch shows one fin looks snapped too"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump (jammed or failed)]\nYes, you do need a new drain pump. The buzzing sound was the motor trying to turn a jammed or broken component. You will need to source a replacement drain pump for your Hoover H3DS4965DACE, which typically involves removing the rear panel and disconnecting the electrical leads and hoses from the old unit before fitting the new one."
  }
 ],
